==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|slipperie}}, an extended form ({{suf|en||-y|id2=adjectival}}) of {{der|en|enm|slipper}}, {{m|enm|sliper|t=slippery}}, from {{der|en|ang|slipor|t=slippery}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*slipraz|t=smooth, slippery}}, equivalent to {{af|en|slip|-er|nocat=1}}. Compare also {{cog|enm|slibbri}}, {{m|enm|slubbri|t=slippery}} borrowed from Middle Dutch or {{cog|gml|slibberich|t=slippery}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|schlüpfrig|t=slippery}}, {{cog|da|slibrig|t=slippery}}, {{cog|sv|slipprig|t=slippery}}.

